{
	"$description": "How a coop's cap table forms. Invested hearts are not burned: they convert one for one into maiaHEARTS, the city's common currency, which the coop's treasury holds to build with. In return the investor receives the coop's MINDs — its ownership currency. Milestones are counted in MINDs: milestone n is reached when the total supply is the n-th Fibonacci number of MINDs — 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13 … — so it emits the difference to the milestone before, at a price of 10 × n hearts per MIND. The earliest believers pay the least per MIND; everyone inside one milestone pays the same price, like a round.",
	"emission": {
		"$description": "Of every MIND minted, this share goes to the investor; the rest to the coop's treasury. The treasury is already paid — it holds the maiaHEARTS — so the MINDs, the ownership, go to the people who backed it.",
		"toInvestor": 1.0,
		"toTreasury": 0.0
	},
	"milestones": {
		"$description": "Milestone n is filled when the total supply reaches fib(n) MINDs; it emits fib(n) − fib(n−1) MINDs at 10 × n hearts each — 10♥ in milestone 1, 20♥ in 2 — and opens once every earlier milestone is filled. The schedule runs until the max supply of 8 billion MINDs: the last milestone emits only what is left under the cap, then the coop is sold out. A coop's total supply is always exactly what its milestones have emitted so far. The table is generated from the rule by scripts/coops-table.ts.",
		"rule": "total(n) = min(fib(n), maxSupply); minds(n) = total(n) - total(n-1); heartsPerMind(n) = n * heartsPerMindStep; cost(n) = minds(n) * heartsPerMind(n)",
		"heartsPerMindStep": "10",
		"maxSupplyMinds": "8000000000",
